{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The screws, acrylic sheets, and magnets fit my recent interest in assembling and fastening parts: they offer hardware, workable material, and removable closures for small builds.",
    "The quick-setting glue complements my epoxy and adhesive tapes for holding small parts during assembly, while the magnetic hooks could help organize the tools I have accumulated if my metal surfaces support them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The roof sealant and bathroom caulk involve adhesives, but filling and weatherproofing seams serves a different purpose from bonding parts during assembly; I have no current sealing project.",
    "The pressure gauge, breadboards, and PEX valves require particular pressure-measurement, electronics, or plumbing projects. Owning measuring tools and fabrication supplies does not give me a reason to use those items now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in tools seems to have been stretched into an interest in almost any repair or workshop supply, even when it requires a project I am not doing.",
    "My adhesive purchases seem to have been treated as a broad interest in sticky or sealing products, without enough attention to what I want to join and how I want to join it."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of rivets, rivet nuts, bolts, screws, and grommet tools point toward making and joining parts, which makes compatible fasteners and materials especially useful.",
    "Practical fit matters: hooks need suitable metal surfaces, screws need appropriate dimensions, and materials need to suit my tools and intended build. A related product is useful only when I can put it to work."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my hands-on assembly interests but extended them too broadly into specialized repair tasks that I have no current reason to undertake."
}"}
